## How it works tabs: business-friendly diagrams

Context: The Patterns, Communities and Scenarios How it works tabs were too
technical for business users. Each tab now leads with plain-language steps,
an energy & utilities example (customers, contracts, meters, sites) and
inline SVG concept diagrams; the previous algorithm text is kept in a
collapsed "Technical details" section. Removed the non-existent "Class"
scenario scope from the copy, and aligned the Compare wording with the
actual "View difference" button.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/intelligence/_intel_patterns_saved.html
   Business walkthrough with two diagrams (looking around a customer by
   hops; grouping look-alikes into patterns with min support), plain-word
   settings, uses; technical text moved into `<details class="howto-tech">`.
2. src/front/templates/partials/intelligence/_intel_communities.html
   Business walkthrough with two diagrams (three grid communities with rare
   bridging links; label propagation in three steps), usage steps, typical
   uses, Patterns vs Communities; technical text collapsed.
